;(Talk to Sampo)
:'''Sampo:''' Bored? Your big brother Sampo's always up for a chat.
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Who the heck are you?
::'''Sampo:''' What kind of question is that!? I'm your old pal &mdash; Sampo Koski &mdash; we've been through thick and thin together!
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You didn't answer the question.
:::'''Sampo:''' Well, that just means there's something wrong with your question! Questions are like transactions &mdash; if your request isn't clear, you might end up buying the wrong thing.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We haven't been through thick OR thin... pal.
:::'''Sampo:''' What do you mean!? We battled wind and snow &mdash; fought shoulder to shoulder against the great Gepard Landau! I risked life and limb in the Fragmentum to save you from the evil clutches of the fearsome Bronya Rand!
:::'''Sampo:''' How's that for thick and thin?
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} My old pal!
:::'''Sampo:''' Yeah! Haha... Wait, do you mean it?
::;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Who are Wildfire and Seele?
::'''Sampo:''' Wildfire are one of my major clients, though the work is mostly odds and ends... Still! It's always a pleasure. Haha, who am I to complain if the money's right, huh?
::'''Sampo:''' Seele works for them &mdash; Oleg's most trusted lieutenant. *sigh* To her I'm probably just, uh, Wildfire's lapdog.
::'''Sampo:''' Haha! But a very contented lapdog, I should add! Hehe...
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} What do Wildfire want?
::'''Sampo:''' As a non-member, not a clue. They'd never tell me their ultimate aims. Shame, really, it's not like I'm a blabbermouth...
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Good to chat.
::'''Sampo:''' A pleasure! Until next time.

;(Talk to Dan Heng)
:'''Dan Heng:''' How are you finding your first Trailblazing expedition?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Pretty great, I enjoy a good adventure!
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...That's good.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I feel a bit discombobulated.
::'''Dan Heng:''' All journeys contain their share of the unexpected. It won't be the last time.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Trailblazing expedition? Pretty unremarkable.
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...Sounds like you've taken it in your stride.
:'''Dan Heng:''' I'm about to summarize the intel we've gathered so far. Did you want to listen?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's why I'm here.
::'''Dan Heng:''' First we have the Underworld &mdash; a huge underground space. Miners have built towns here and are excavating Geomarrow.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What's the relation between here and the Overworld?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' We learned from Natasha that the Underworld shoulders the energy needs of their entire civilization. Laboring in the Underworld used to be a great honor, and there was regular movement between realms.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' Sampo mentioned the Furnace Core, which people would use to travel in both directions. Yet now, each realm is sealed off from the other. Only the automatic transport line for Geomarrow and goods is still in operation.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' The reason for sealing the Furnace Core still needs to be investigated. In addition, it appears that Sampo has secret connections that grant him passage between here and the surface. That may come in useful to us.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Do soldiers from the Overworld ever come down here?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' Up to now, apart from Bronya, whom Sampo brought here, I still haven't seen a single Silvermane Guard.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' At the Fight Club I heard people say that the Guards withdrew from the underground many years ago, and that it was the supreme guardian who gave the order.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' At the time, the supreme guardian was none other than Cocolia Rand.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm clear on this bit. What else?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' Next we have our goal &mdash; the Stellaron.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' After we revealed our intentions, the supreme guardian suspended communications and sent soldiers to arrest us. Her reaction was strange, to say the least.
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why did the supreme guardian choose to act that way?
::::'''Dan Heng:''' It's too early to say, but it was a radical move. It means that we must have broached a highly sensitive subject... a secret that she's sparing no effort to protect.
::::'''Dan Heng:''' If I remember our discussion correctly, I think there are two main possibilities: The Architects, and the Stellaron. I'm inclined to think it's the latter, but we lack evidence.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Will we find any Stellaron clues in the Underworld?
::::'''Dan Heng:''' There's an old saying that goes: "Good fortune lies within bad, bad fortune lurks within good." Even when compared with the Overworld, the Underworld has a long history. There should be valuable intel here. Not to mention, without the supreme guardian's interference, we have a better chance than ever of locating the Stellaron.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} Uhh, maybe next time.
::'''Dan Heng:''' No problem, come find me any time.

;(Talk to March 7th)
:'''March 7th:''' Oh, hi (Trailblazer), wanna listen to my thoughts on the underground?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sure.
::'''March 7th:''' Where should I start?
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} I want to hear about your observations....
:::'''March 7th:''' Ha, my observational skills are second to none.
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} How about the Underworld geography?
::::'''March 7th:''' Well, the Underworld is surrounded by cliffs, and there's no obvious structure. It seems like a spread out collection of mines and small towns &mdash; just like the outskirts of Belobog.
::::'''March 7th:''' There's that huge pillar called the Furnace Core that's always in view &mdash; maybe it's some kind of energy hub?
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} How about Underworld life?
::::'''March 7th:''' From what I've seen, the residents are nearly all miners. It seems like the people here have less than those in the Overworld.
::::'''March 7th:''' Still, the miners watch fights in their spare time. It's less pretentious than that theater they have on the surface.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} How about the Underworlders?
::::'''March 7th:''' They're always in a hurry. The pace of life here is so fast! Things are pretty busy in the Overworld too, but everything feels more relaxed up there.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} That's all I can think of.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} I want to hear what you think about the others...
:::'''March 7th:''' I'm not so good at analyzing people, but seeing as you asked...
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Sampo?
::::'''March 7th:''' That guy!? He's lazy, lying, cunning, and evil! I don't like him &mdash; can't stand the sight of him.
::::'''March 7th:''' I bet you think he's pretty entertaining. Watch out, or he'll fool you!
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Hook?
::::'''March 7th:''' Ah, you mean that naughty kid we played hide-and-seek with?
::::'''March 7th:''' Dr. Natasha said that she's a handful, but that she also takes care of the homeless kids. Maybe she's more mature than she seems?
::::'''March 7th:''' ...Still, I can't believe how arrogant she is. I was pretty mad with her for a while.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Bronya?
::::'''March 7th:''' The Silvermane girl? She's pretty. I like looking at her.
::::'''March 7th:''' When I first met her I thought she was kinda scary, but now it seems like there's something on her mind. I'm too nervous to ask her.
::::'''March 7th:''' At least she's not trying to arrest us anymore.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Seele?
::::'''March 7th:''' She says what she thinks &mdash; I like her. And did you hear what she said about the Silvermane Guards? Haha, sounded like she'd been waiting a long time to say it. I think I'd get along with her.
::::'''March 7th:''' If we can get her to help us, we'll bag a Stellaron in no time!
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's all I can think of.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's it for now.
:::'''March 7th:''' If you hear any juicy gossi&mdash; uh... information, come find me!
:{{Диалог|Выход}} Not right now.
::'''March 7th:''' No worries, just thought you might be interested.

;(Talk to Bronya)
:'''Bronya:''' ...I will arrest you under the supreme guardian's decree. Nothing has changed.
:'''Bronya:''' I am not your friend...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It takes time to make friends.
::'''Bronya:''' ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I like to get close to my enemies.
::'''Bronya:''' ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Please arrest me! I can't wait!
::'''Bronya:''' ...There's... something wrong with you.
:'''Bronya:''' ...I saw you the day before the Goethe Hotel. Gepard took you to see mo&mdash; ...the supreme guardian. He told me you were visitors from beyond the sky.
:'''Bronya:''' Just like the interstellar travelers of ancient legend &mdash; people of all kinds that carried the will of the Aeons.
:'''Bronya:''' Gepard said that you wanted to help us reverse the damage that the Eternal Freeze and Fragmentum continue to wreak on our planet... but that night, mother summoned me, and ordered me to take a detachment to arrest you.
:'''Bronya:''' What happened? The supreme guardian didn't tell me the details and Gepard had to rush back to the front line... I don't understand...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're not the only one...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We really do want to help you.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The supreme guardian betrayed us.
:'''Bronya:''' ...
:'''Bronya:''' The Silvermane Guards withdrew to the surface long ago... I must avoid that identity here.
:'''Bronya:''' Until we're back in the Overworld, I propose a temporary truce and cooperation. Your true intentions are of interest to me...
:'''Bronya:''' If it helps you to trust me, I'm willing to answer your questions to the best of my ability.
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} What crime have we committed?
::'''Bronya:''' Let me repeat &mdash; all I received were the supreme guardian's instructions. It is for the adjudication panel to pass judgment on the accused.
::'''Bronya:''' ...All the supreme guardian told me was that your identities were counterfeit, and that your intention was to overthrow the rule of the Architects.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Do you know where the Stellaron is?
::'''Bronya:''' Truthfully, I've never heard of this Stellaron.
::'''Bronya:''' But if all this catastrophe could be brought to an end simply by sealing it, then I hope its existence proves to be real.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why did the Silvermane Guards withdraw from the underground?
::'''Bronya:''' Fragmentum monster activity on the surface intensified, and hostilities on the front line were critical. To resist the invasion, the Architects had no choice but to redeploy the Guards to the front line.
::'''Bronya:''' ...If we couldn't hold our defensive line, then we wouldn't be able to maintain our supply of aid to the underground, which would have collapsed without us. That was the supreme guardian's explanation.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why are you willing to cooperate with us?
::'''Bronya:''' In truth... I've always felt like something important is being hidden. Whether it's the Architects, mother, or Silvermane Guards, there's always an... unnatural element to their actions.
::'''Bronya:''' Since encountering you, the unexpected seems to have arrived in waves. I never thought I'd enter the Underworld that has been sealed away for so long...
::'''Bronya:''' I have a feeling that with you, I can pick up the lost threads... and dispel my uncertainties.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's all I have to ask.
::'''Bronya:''' Mm, we should be going to see Wildfire. Let's move.
{{Dialogue End}}

